.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH note 1  "note " 
.SH NAME
note \- Add or list notes (the change/worklog stream) on an item
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnote\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add or list notes (the change/worklog stream) on an item
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
note\-add(1)
Append a note to an item. Pass `\-` as the text to read the note body from STDIN (escaping\-free, multi\-line)
.TP
note\-list(1)
List an item\*(Aqs notes
.TP
note\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
